{"title":"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Properties_of_Logarithms)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Properties of Logarithms)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Properties_of_Logarithms)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Properties of Logarithms)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#First,_we_can_get_rid_of_the_exponents_using_properties_of_logarithms\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">First, we can get rid of the  exponents using properties of logarithms</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Estimations_and_Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Estimations and Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Properties_of_Logarithms)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Properties of Logarithms)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Using_Logarithmic_Manipulations)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using Logarithmic Manipulations)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath_(Using_Magical_Ability)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath (Using Magical Ability)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by The Power of Logic</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Logic_and_Simplification)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Logic and Simplification)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/3/9934e0771c30ad96de59aa26766c6befd3570ccd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{20} \\log_{5^k} 3^{k^2}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{100} \\log_{9^k} 25^k\\right)?\\]\" width=\"263\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/b/4cb12065097b0e72e7b9094e519692ffb17eeb82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }21 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }100\\log_5 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }200\\log_3 5 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }2{,}200\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }21{,}000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"567\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Properties_of_Logarithms.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Properties_of_Logarithms)\">Solution 1 (Properties of Logarithms)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Properties of Logarithms)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will apply the following logarithmic identity:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0ea4c6c73797a08783331e929de21aa39301cc2f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{p^n}{q^n}=\\log_{p}{q},\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"19\" />\nwhich can be proven by the Change of Base Formula: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef085f640a32dbc3335a1534ab28e420210bb84b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{p^n}{q^n}=\\frac{\\log_{p}{q^n}}{\\log_{p}{p^n}}=\\frac{n\\log_{p}{q}}{n}=\\log_{p}{q}.\\]\" width=\"296\" height=\"45\" />\nNow, we simplify the expressions inside the summations:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f824183bf5f17eed210357b92fb4b0315c50d53.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\log_{5^k}{{3^k}^2}&amp;=\\log_{5^k}{(3^k)^k} \\\\ &amp;=k\\log_{5^k}{3^k} \\\\ &amp;=k\\log_{5}{3}, \\end{align*}\" width=\"169\" height=\"76\" />\nand \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36cf5e78f24ad53ba00870a39c1b50085f04519b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\log_{9^k}{25^k}&amp;=\\log_{3^{2k}}{5^{2k}} \\\\ &amp;=\\log_{3}{5}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"161\" height=\"45\" />\nUsing these results, we evaluate the original expression:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edff5ef8c280d28c288365044a6cf6ecc5d3793b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{20} \\log_{5^k} 3^{k^2}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{100} \\log_{9^k} 25^k\\right)&amp;=\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{20} k\\log_{5}{3}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{100} \\log_{3}{5}\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\left(\\log_{5}{3}\\cdot\\sum_{k=1}^{20} k\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\log_{3}{5}\\cdot\\sum_{k=1}^{100} 1\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{20} k\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{100} 1\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{21\\cdot20}{2}\\cdot100 \\\\ &amp;= \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }21{,}000}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"533\" height=\"253\" />\n~MRENTHUSIASM (Solution)\n</p><p>~JHawk0224 (Proposal)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Properties_of_Logarithms.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Properties_of_Logarithms)\">Solution 2 (Properties of Logarithms)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Properties of Logarithms)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span id=\"First.2C_we_can_get_rid_of_the_exponents_using_properties_of_logarithms\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"First,_we_can_get_rid_of_the_exponents_using_properties_of_logarithms\">First, we can get rid of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> exponents using properties of logarithms</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: First, we can get rid of the  exponents using properties of logarithms\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/7/d375198a7ced5b7ad3fc2e82a72fa23cf6f915d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{5^k} 3^{k^2} = k^2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{k} \\cdot \\log_{5} 3 = k\\log_{5} 3 = \\log_{5} 3^k.\\]\" width=\"349\" height=\"37\" /> (Leaving the single <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> in the exponent will come in handy later). Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/8/19863447b7c09181a04d4427bb1ef0eb0505a7dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{9^k} 25^{k} = k \\cdot \\frac{1}{k} \\cdot \\log_{9} 25 = \\log_{9} 5^2.\\]\" width=\"272\" height=\"37\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>Then, evaluating the first few terms in each parentheses, we can find the simplified expanded forms of each sum using the additive property of logarithms:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/3/5b36ccc0cf9ab8b6ec5a5fc585de769c40a0a960.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sum_{k=1}^{20} \\log_{5} 3^k &amp;= \\log_{5} 3^1 + \\log_{5} 3^2 + \\dots + \\log_{5} 3^{20} \\\\ &amp;= \\log_{5} 3^{(1 + 2 + \\dots + 20)} \\\\ &amp;= \\log_{5} 3^{\\frac{20(20+1)}{2}} &amp;&amp;\\hspace{15mm}(*) \\\\ &amp;= \\log_{5} 3^{210}, \\\\ \\sum_{k=1}^{100} \\log_{9} 5^2 &amp;= \\log_{9} 5^2 + \\log_{9} 5^2 + \\dots + \\log_{9} 5^2 \\\\ &amp;= \\log_{9} 5^{2(100)} \\\\ &amp;= \\log_{9} 5^{200}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"458\" height=\"256\" />\nIn <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63fc5c700c9ef6c6097f086c2d1db5db8e9d3f65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(*),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> we use the triangular numbers equation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/2/9920a14a6b5485fd9729778777568ddc51983c64.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 + 2 + \\dots + n = \\frac{n(n+1)}{2} = \\frac{20(20+1)}{2} = 210.\\]\" width=\"375\" height=\"38\" />\nFinally, multiplying the two logarithms together, we can use the chain rule property of logarithms to simplify:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/4/dc4e62f569fbc51cb808fe98f458e471341e9ea8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{a} b\\log_{x} y = \\log_{a} y\\log_{x} b.\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"17\" />\nThus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4cd5e0e9c15103049b5e37d474c92ac048a9a75.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\left(\\log_{5} 3^{210}\\right)\\left(\\log_{3^2} 5^{200}\\right) &amp;= \\left(\\log_{5} 5^{200}\\right)\\left(\\log_{3^2} 3^{210}\\right) \\\\ &amp;= \\left(\\log_{5} 5^{200}\\right)\\left(\\log_{3} 3^{105}\\right) \\\\ &amp;= (200)(105) \\\\ &amp;= \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }21{,}000}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"358\" height=\"111\" />\n~Joeya (Solution)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Evaluate\n\\[\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{20}\\log_{5^k}3^{k^2}\\right)\n\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{100}\\log_{9^k}25^k\\right).\\]\n</p><p>Apply change of base:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/f/34f43610c42dfb357e3e9bf022583d93dc44d550.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{a^m}b^n=\\frac nm\\log_a b.\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>For the first sum,\\[\n\\log_{5^k}3^{k^2}\n=\\frac{k^2}{k}\\log_5 3\n=k\\log_5 3.\\]\n</p><p>Hence\n\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{20}\\log_{5^k}3^{k^2}\n=\\frac{20(21)}2\\log_5 3\n=210\\log_5 3.\\]\n</p><p>For the second,\n\\[\\log_{9^k}25^k\n=\\log_9 25\n=\\log_3 5.\\]\n</p><p>Therefore,\n\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{100}\\log_{9^k}25^k\n=100\\log_3 5.\\]\n</p><p>Multiply:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/419989dfcb5e4ad9fe028f57629493e247ea93d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[21000(\\log_5 3)(\\log_3 5).\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>But\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/6/6268c254470a6e9fe93922f7d3e71ef6cf826982.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\log_a b\\cdot\\log_b a=1}.\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"29\" />\n</p><p>Thus the answer is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/e/2ced4ffe1954995a11a7724c2cb5ad07cbe855c7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\text{E. }21000}.\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Focus the inner term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd3222500f94ca0d42eca6336b4fbaa4a0807006.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{5^k}(3^{k^{2}})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"24\" />. That is,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/2/9023e67a457d177b67e5cf63a800f4c99d0e783f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{k} \\cdot \\log_{5}(3^{k^{2}})\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a1957454efb028e4b8748d871cac6276ac4503d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= k \\log_{5}(3)\\]\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>The sum becomes\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eefb8569dac872818b3b9c1c4f5ca55a54d59f69.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{5}(3) \\cdot \\sum_{k=1}^{20} k = 210 \\log_{5}(3)\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p>Focus the next inner term, particularly\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3a4b7ff8174dce53510edc4956673251c9b29b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{9^k}(25^k)\\]\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/5/185392c1e96a8bcd609681334833f07df8a0b4bf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{1}{k} \\cdot \\log_9(25^k)\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/3/07392714c52d0df94839270ee8df1f241b7a1f7e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\log_9(25)\\]\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>So the sum becomes\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2af0e8afbafc71015ba4013d615bfdd57482ca5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{100} \\log_9(25) = 100\\log_9(25) = 200\\log_9(5) = 100\\log_3(5)\\]\" width=\"425\" height=\"51\" />.\n</p><p>So we desire\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/b/97b7448631bc1ae6805a8d48ef535ad7e5d584ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[210 \\log_{5}(3) \\cdot 100\\log_3(5)\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/6802c0cd80aa43d81523be62334589729ff09823.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{210}{\\log_3(5)} \\cdot 100 \\log_3(5)\\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/4/3a438a6e2c8949ef675a1c20b9aeddde22d69735.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 210 \\cdot 100\\]\" width=\"85\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/036bceb8419fb5c4489c3f2d37d5b8c3c296268f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\boxed{21000}\\]\" width=\"75\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Estimations_and_Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Estimations_and_Answer_Choices)\">Solution 4 (Estimations and Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Estimations and Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d654d4d2fd846b05fde297a06a24148a94e228f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{20} \\log_{5^k} 3^{k^2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"97\" height=\"50\" /> note that the addends are greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c196eae3e2f54257197d87215490e1263944b644.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\geq2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/9/a099dabcc10b785e7602049e9bc82a3e1147cd78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{100} \\log_{9^k} 25^k,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"103\" height=\"56\" /> note that the addends are greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/2/ff2aa9f06706d0ec4a5f92c49f70912a0f585394.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\geq1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We have the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2e06105e0de5a91367d985665fd86180510a95e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{20} \\log_{5^k} 3^{k^2}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{100} \\log_{9^k} 25^k\\right)&gt;\\left(\\sum_{k=2}^{20} 1\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{100} 1\\right)=19\\cdot100=1{,}900,\\]\" width=\"552\" height=\"53\" /> which eliminates choices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/3/8d384e7cea1a848fce02b68a8bc4d4bbb333e2ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}, \\textbf{(B)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/7/f07759fa176d8edab201426b075c105d704ff275.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"17\" /> We get the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f20fc268163e5f05dbfe0c0948cf4c4121b04aba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }21{,}000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"97\" height=\"30\" /> by either an educated guess or a continued approximation: \n</p><p>Observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/7/4e7a30c84da003f4357ac64905b43a166910abc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{20} \\log_{5^k} 3^{k^2} &gt;&gt; \\sum_{k=2}^{20} 1 = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"214\" height=\"56\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc7fbcf63b45c31d2ab4f305841aab1b287e3d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{100} \\log_{9^k} 25^k\\approx\\sum_{k=1}^{100} \\log_{9^k} 27^k = \\sum_{k=1}^{100} \\frac{3}{2} = 150.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"341\" height=\"56\" /> Therefore, we obtain the following rough underestimation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/6/656fb2569c7ac2ee53e271fe054033cf2c5f921e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{20} \\log_{5^k} 3^{k^2}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{100} \\log_{9^k} 25^k\\right)&gt;\\left(\\sum_{k=2}^{20} 1\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{100} \\frac{3}{2}\\right)=19\\cdot150=2{,}850.\\]\" width=\"556\" height=\"53\" />\nFrom here, it should be safe to guess that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/5729ea372cb53da5f2596d6f802dbd34914d4322.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Properties_of_Logarithms.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Properties_of_Logarithms)\">Solution 5 (Properties of Logarithms)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Properties of Logarithms)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0ea4c6c73797a08783331e929de21aa39301cc2f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{p^n}{q^n}=\\log_{p}{q},\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"19\" /> simplify <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34a0661d56e42489ce5d5cc7e87ae0b90d90cc59.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\log_{5^k}{{3^k}^2}&amp;=\\log_{5^k}{(3^k)^k} \\\\ &amp;=\\log_{5}{3^k} \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"169\" height=\"52\" />\nand \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36cf5e78f24ad53ba00870a39c1b50085f04519b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\log_{9^k}{25^k}&amp;=\\log_{3^{2k}}{5^{2k}} \\\\ &amp;=\\log_{3}{5}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"161\" height=\"45\" />. Now we have the product: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/7/bd74dab6131d94c5973f8b727b73735e9c61319f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{20} \\log_{5} 3^{k}\\right)\\cdot\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^{100} \\log_{3} 5\\right)\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"53\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/9096ad38af341aca3a5cb2a7e2d3f39ed204bbde.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sum_{k=1}^{20} \\log_{5} 3^k &amp;= \\log_{5} 3^1 + \\log_{5} 3^2 + \\dots + \\log_{5} 3^{20} \\\\ &amp;= \\log_{5} 3^{(1 + 2 + \\dots + 20)} \\\\ &amp;= \\log_{5} 3^{\\frac{20(20+1)}{2}} \\\\ &amp;= \\log_{5} 3^{210} \\\\ &amp;= {210}\\cdot\\log_{5} {3}, \\\\ \\sum_{k=1}^{100}\\log_{3} {5} &amp;= {100}\\cdot\\log_{3} {5}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"348\" height=\"225\" /> \nWith the reciprocal rule the logarithms cancel out leaving: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/065047ef45a30c540ce5f876e6487906bb4ac818.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }21{,}000}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"102\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:PowerQualimit\" title=\"User:PowerQualimit\">PowerQualimit</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=FD9BE7hpRvg&amp;t=322s\">https://youtube.com/watch?v=FD9BE7hpRvg&amp;t=322s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Hawk Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AjQARBvdZ20\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AjQARBvdZ20</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_.28Using_Logarithmic_Manipulations.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Using_Logarithmic_Manipulations)\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using Logarithmic Manipulations)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using Logarithmic Manipulations)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/vgFPZ-hyd-I\">https://youtu.be/vgFPZ-hyd-I</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath_.28Using_Magical_Ability.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath_(Using_Magical_Ability)\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath (Using Magical Ability)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath (Using Magical Ability)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ySWSHyY9TwI?t=999\">https://youtu.be/ySWSHyY9TwI?t=999</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_The_Power_of_Logic\">Video Solution by The Power of Logic</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by The Power of Logic\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/b7xEeR7HXkE\">https://youtu.be/b7xEeR7HXkE</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Logic_and_Simplification.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Logic_and_Simplification)\">Video Solution (Logic and Simplification)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Logic and Simplification)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/F6w9zsiMZ8w\">https://youtu.be/F6w9zsiMZ8w</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A\">2021 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2